From: RM01 HAOS port <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3568-jl-rm01: disable NPU during HAOS bring-up

The BSP's NPU power-management path panics early on this hardware while
running the HAOS kernel userspace.  Keep the NPU disabled until that BSP
issue is understood.  This does not affect CPU, eMMC, SD, Ethernet, USB,
or display bring-up.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-jl-rm01.dtsi | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-jl-rm01.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-jl-rm01.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-jl-rm01.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-jl-rm01.dtsi
@@ -272,17 +272,17 @@
 
 &rknpu {
 	rknpu-supply = <&vdd_npu>;
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &rknpu_mmu {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &bus_npu {
 	bus-supply = <&vdd_logic>;
 	pvtm-supply = <&vdd_cpu>;
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &vdpu {
-- 
2.43.0

